    "title": "pandas.IntervalIndex.set_closed — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.IntervalIndex.set_closed#\n\n- \nIntervalIndex.set_closed(*closed* )[source]#\n- Return an identical IntervalArray closed on the specified side. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **closed** {‘left’, ‘right’, ‘both’, ‘neither’}\n    - Whether the intervals are closed on the left-side, right-side, both or neither.\n  - Returns:\n    - IntervalArray\n    - A new IntervalArray with the specified side closures.\n See also \n  - `IntervalArray.closed`\n  - Returns inclusive side of the Interval.\n  - `arrays.IntervalArray.closed`\n  - Returns inclusive side of the IntervalArray.\n Examples >>> index = pd.arrays.IntervalArray.from_breaks(range(4)) >>> index <IntervalArray> [(0, 1], (1, 2], (2, 3]] Length: 3, dtype: interval[int64, right] >>> index.set_closed(\"both\") <IntervalArray> [[0, 1], [1, 2], [2, 3]] Length: 3, dtype: interval[int64, both]",
    "markdown_length": 834,
